  "notes": "West leads the ♦K against 4♠. The North-South club holding looks tailor made for an elimination. South must try to eliminate hearts and diamonds without allowing East on lead. A club lead from East will destroy the elimination.\n\nSouth should trade his 2 heart losers, which East may be able to win, for 2 diamond losers, which only West can win. South begins by allowing West to hold the opening lead.\n\nWest will switch to hearts, but South can win the ♥A. Trumps are drawn, ending in the South hand and the ♦A is cashed for a heart discard. The ♦J is played, covered by West as the last heart is pitched from North.\n\nWest will return a heart, ruffed in dummy. South crosses in trumps and plays his last heart ruffing in dummy. Hearts and diamonds are now removed and a trump still exists in both hands. A club is played from North. Whatever East plays, South covers as cheaply as possible. West may win, but he will be endplayed.",
